  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "North Lakeville’s name simply tells you its location—‘North’ for its position north of Lakeville, and ‘Lakeville’ for its lakeside roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/north-lakeville-152912",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before Europeans arrived, the area that is now North Lakeville was part of the traditional lands of the Wampanoag people.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/north-lakeville-152912",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "North Lakeville sits within Plymouth County, a region famous for being the site of the first English settlement in New England, Plymouth Colony.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/north-lakeville-152912",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "North Lakeville is an unincorporated village that lies within the town limits of Lakeville in southeastern Massachusetts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/north-lakeville-152912",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Although it has no major tourist sites, North Lakeville benefits from nearby cranberry bogs that are a key part of the region’s agricultural heritage.",
